+# Slice 3.RV-markdown — fix round 1
+
+Board "Review a commit range" row 11. Original brief: `briefs/3.RV-markdown.md` (its Contract stands). Your round-1
+patch is committed (`ae46983`); the reviews are `.omp/run/notes/RVMarkdownBoundary.md` and
+`.omp/run/notes/RVMarkdownCorrect.md` — read both in full, their probes and numbers are given. Owned is widened to the
+shared homes they name. The range window's fence rules (PM9) are in `fences.ts` since `50444c3`: keep them.
+
+## Target
+
+Owned: `frontend/src/editor/markdown.ts`, `frontend/src/editor/internal/{markdownBlocks,markdownInline,markdownDom,
+codeBlock,removalTooltip,language,syntax}.ts` and their `.test.ts` files (new or changed),
+`frontend/src/editor/internal/markdownDom.browser.test.ts`, `frontend/src/ui/useMarkdown.ts`,
+`frontend/src/ui/useMarkdown.test.ts` (new), `frontend/scripts/{fences,fences.test,markdownFence,markdownFence.test}.ts`
+(`markdownFence*` new).
+
+Read-only: everything else.
+
+## Blocks to fix (verbatim from the reviews; 1–5 are blocks, the rest promoted)
+
+1. **One highlighter for code outside a pane** (`codeBlock.ts:25`, plan #102): `highlighted()` and `HIGHLIGHTERS` copy
+   `removalTooltip.ts:27–42`. Export one `highlightedNodes(document, code, parser): Node[]` holding the highlighter
+   pair (in `codeBlock.ts` or beside the table in `syntax.ts`); `paintCode` and `removalTooltip.ts` both call it.
+2. **Bounded nesting** (`markdownBlocks.ts:200`, `:240`, `markdownInline.ts:127`): one `MAX_NESTING` (e.g. 16) passed
+   through `blocksOf`/`quote`/`list` and through the inline recursion; past it the rest is literal paragraph text.
+   Node tests: a 10,000-deep quote, list and emphasis each parse to text without throwing.
+3. **Linear heading match** (`markdownBlocks.ts:34–35`): match `/^ {0,3}(#{1,6})(?:[ \t]+(.*))?$/`, then `trimEnd()`
+   the content and drop a trailing `#` run only when a space or tab precedes it, with string operations instead of
+   `HEADING_CLOSE`. Node test: a heading with 100,000 inner spaces parses to its text (time it; report).
+4. **Linear inline scanning** (`markdownInline.ts:106`, `:176`): replace the rescanning `closer` with one left-to-right
+   delimiter stack per inline run (CommonMark's process_emphasis with `openers_bottom`, linear); remember the first
+   position past which no `]`/`)` closes, so a later `[`/`(` answers literal without scanning. Node tests: `*a `×20000
+   and `[](`×20000 parse (time them; report).
