+   !interrupts(lines, end)` instead of `includes("|")`. Node test: a quote with a pipe right after a table starts a
+   quote.
+6. **One language load-and-log** (`codeBlock.ts:56`): pull the load-and-log out of `language.ts` as
+   `loadedSupport(description, fields): Promise<LanguageSupport | null>` with the one event name; `loadLanguage` and
+   `paintCode` both use it.
+7. **The MarkdownView fence in its own file** (`fences.ts:129`, at 287/300 lines): move `namesOf`,
+   `exposesMarkdownView`, `markdownViolations` and their constants into `scripts/markdownFence.ts`, exporting
+   `markdownViolations` as `clipboardFence.ts` does; `fences.ts` calls it.
+8. **No swappable positional strings** (`markdownDom.ts:4`, TS7): pass the code block itself (`paint(element, block:
+   Extract<Block, { kind: "code" }>)`, `codeNode(document, block, paint)`), and give `textElement`/`withInlines` an
+   options object `{ tag, className, text }`.
